/9.\nThe answer is 4/9 or 44.44%.\n\nAnswer_14:\nJenna's mom got 20 apples.\nJenna picked half as many apples as her mom.\nSo Jenna picked 20 / 2 = 10 apples.\nThe answer is 10.\n\nAnswer_15:\nThe rats are kept in 3 cages in equal groups.\nEach rat is given 6 pieces of straw.\nLet's say there are x rats in each cage.\nThen the total number of rats is 3x.\nThe total number of straw given to the rats is 6 * 3x = 18x.\nThe hamsters are kept alone, so each hamster gets 5 pieces of straw.\nThere are 10 cages of hamsters, so the total number of straw given to the hamsters is 5 * 10 = 50.\nThe total number of straw given to the small rodents is 160.\nSo 18x + 50 = 160.\n18x = 110.\nx = 110 / 18 = 6.11.\nSince you can't have a fraction of a rat, there must be 6 rats in each cage.\nThe answer is 6.\n\nAnswer_16:\nMandy owes Benedict $100.\nThey agreed to have monthly interest of 2%.\nThe interest for the first month is 2% of $100 = 0.02 * 100 = $2.\nThe interest for the second month is 2% of $102 = 0.02 * 102 = $2.04.\nThe interest for the third month is 2% of $104.04 = 0.02 * 104.04 = $2.08.\nThe total interest is $2 + $2.04 + $2.08 = $6.12.\nThe total amount Mandy needs to pay is $100 + $6.12 = $106.12.\nThe answer is $106.12.\n\nAnswer_17:\nThe trader buys bags of wheat at $20 each.\nHe sells them at $30 each.\nThe profit per bag is $30 - $20 = $10.\nThe total profit is $400.\nThe number of bags sold is $400 / $10 = 40.\nThe answer is 40.\n\nAnswer_18:\nThree friends spent $20.25 on 3 tickets to the fair.\nThey also spent $4.50 less on food than on the tickets.\nSo they spent $20.25 - $4.50 = $15.75 on food.\nThey also went on 2 different rides which costs $33 for each ride.\nSo they spent $33 * 2 = $66 on rides.\nThe total amount spent is $20.25 + $15.75 + $66 = $102.\nThey agreed to split all the costs evenly.\nSo each of them paid $102 / 3 = $34.\nThe answer is $34.\n\nAnswer_19:\nJohn collects peaches for 3 hours.\nHe can collect 2 peaches a minute.\nSo he collects 2 * 60 = 120 peaches in an hour.\nIn 3 hours, he collects 120 * 3 = 360 peaches.\nThe answer is 360.\n\nAnswer_20:\nDucks need to eat 3.5 pounds of insects each week.\nThere is a flock of ten ducks.\nSo they need 3.5 * 10 = 35 pounds of insects per week.\nThey need 35 / 7 = 5 pounds of insects per day.\nThe answer is 5.\n\nAnswer_21:\nTom plants 10 trees a year.\nHe also chops down 2 trees a year.\nSo he has 10 - 2 = 8 trees left each year.\nHe starts with 50 trees.\nAfter 10 years, he has 50 * (1 - 2/10) ^ 10 = 50 * (0.8) ^ 10 = 50 * 0.1073741824 = 5.368710912.\nHe has 5.368710912 trees left.\nSince you can't have a fraction of a tree, he has 5 trees left.\n30% of the trees die.\nSo 0.3 * 50 = 15 trees die.\nHe has 50 - 15 = 35 trees left.\nThe answer is 35.\n\nAnswer_22:\nThe neighbors placed 18 pink plastic flamingos out on Sue's front yard.\nOn Saturday morning, they took back one third of the flamingos, painted them white, and put these newly painted white flamingos back out on Sue's front yard.\nSo they took back 18 / 3 = 6 flamingos.\nThey left 18 - 6 = 12 flamingos.\nOn Sunday morning, they added another 18 pink plastic flamingos to the collection.\nSo there are 18 + 12 = 30 pink flamingos.\nThere are 6 white flamingos.\nAt noon on Sunday, there are 30 - 6 = 24 more pink plastic flamingos than white plastic flamingos.\nThe answer is 24.\n\nAnswer_23:\nVioletta needs crayons in 5 different colors.\nOne crayon costs $2.\nShe prepared $20 for this purchase.\nSo she can buy 20 / 2 = 10 crayons.\nThe answer is 10.\n\nAnswer_24:\nA pen costs as much as a pencil and eraser combined.\nA pencil costs $1.20.\nAn eraser costs $0.30.\nSo a pen costs $1.20 + $0.30 = $1.50.\n8 pens will cost 8 * $1.50 = $12.\nThe answer is $12.\n\nAnswer_25:\n200 pounds of carrots are to be distributed to 40 restaurants.\nEach restaurant is to receive 2 pounds of carrots.\nSo the total number of carrots distributed is 40 * 2 = 80 pounds.\nThe number of carrots not used is 200 - 80 = 120 pounds.\nThe answer is 120.\n\nAnswer_26:\nThere are 23786 inhabitants in the city of Soda.\n8417 men and 9092 women make up 8417 + 9092 = 17509 inhabitants.\nThe rest of the population is made up of children.\nSo the number of children is 23786 - 17509 = 6277.\nThe answer is 6277.\n\nAnswer_27:\nElaine initially had 20 Pokemon cards.\nAfter a month, she collected three times that number.\nSo she collected 20 * 3 = 60 cards.\nIn the second month, she collected 20 fewer cards than those she collected in the first month.\nSo she collected 60 - 20 = 40 cards.\nIn the third month, she collected twice the combined number of pokemon cards she collected in the first two months.\nSo she collected 2 * (60 + 40) = 2 * 100 = 200 cards.\nThe total number of cards she has now is 20 + 60 + 40 + 200 = 320.\nThe answer is 320.\n\nAnswer_28:\nMark edits an equal number of sentences each week for two different publishers.\nPublisher B pays Mark twice what Publisher A pays.\nPublisher A pays Mark 5 cents per sentence.\nSo Publisher B pays Mark 10 cents per sentence.\nMark edits a total number of 1000 sentences each week.\nPublisher A pays him 5 cents per sentence, so he gets 5 * 500 = 2500 cents from Publisher A.\nPublisher B pays him 10 cents per sentence, so he gets 10 * 500 = 5000 cents from Publisher B.\nThe total amount Mark makes in a week is 2500 + 5000 = 7500 cents.\nThe answer is 7500.\n\nAnswer_29:\nBaldur gets water from a well.\nHe gets 5 pails of water every morning and 6 pails of water every afternoon.\nSo he gets 5 + 6 = 11 pails of water each day.\nEach pail contains 5 liters of water.\nSo he gets 11 * 5 = 55 liters of water each day.\nThe answer is 55.\n\nAnswer_30:\nJohn wins an award at work.\nThe award has a 1 time monetary reward of $5000.\nHe also gets a 5% raise in salary.\nHe makes $2000 a week.\nSo his annual salary is 2000 * 52 = 104000 dollars.\nA 5% raise is 5% of 104000 = 0.05 * 104000 = 5200 dollars.\nSo his new annual salary is 104000 + 5200 = 109200 dollars.\nHe got the award on the first day of the year.\nSo he worked for 365 days.\nHe made 109200 dollars in a year.\nThe answer is 109200.\n\nAnswer_31:\nJosie grows grapes on her 10-acre farm.\nEach acre produces 5 tons of grapes per year.\nSo the total number of tons of grapes produced is 10 * 5 = 50 tons.\nEach ton of grapes makes 2 barrels of wine.\nSo the total number of barrels of wine produced is 50 * 2 = 100 barrels.\nThe answer is 100.\n\nAnswer_32:\nCarl ate a sandwich every day this week for lunch and used 2 slices of cheese on each sandwich.\nSo he used 2 * 7 = 14 slices of cheese on sandwiches.\nHe ate cheese and egg omelets for breakfast 3 days in the week using one more slice per omelet than he did per sandwich.\nSo he used 2 + 1 = 3 slices of cheese per omelet.\nHe ate 3 omelets, so he used 3 * 3 = 9 slices of cheese on omelets.\nHe made a big dish of macaroni and cheese to last him several dinners for the week and used 8 slices of cheese in it.\nSo he used 14 + 9 + 8 = 31 slices of cheese in total.\nThe answer is 31.\n\nAnswer_33:\nJanet had 22 green pens and 10 yellow pens.\nThen she bought 6 bags of blue pens and 2 bags of red pens.\nThere were 9 pens in each bag of blue and 6 pens in each bag of red.\nSo she bought 6 * 9 = 54 blue pens and 2 * 6 = 12 red pens.\nThe total number of pens she bought is 54 + 12 = 66.\nThe total number of pens she has now is 22 + 10 + 66 = 98.\nThe answer is 98.\n\nAnswer_34:\nBrinley has scores of 89, 71, 92, 100 and 86 on the first five tests.\nShe needs to get an average of 93 on the six tests.\nThe total score she needs is 93 * 6 = 558.\nThe total score she has so far is 89 + 71 + 92 + 100 + 86 = 338.\nThe score she needs on the sixth test is 558 - 338 = 220.\nThe answer is 220.\n\nAnswer_35:\nMicheal rode his bike at least 5 times a week and makes 25 kilometers each time.\nSo he rode 5 * 25 = 125 kilometers each week.\nHe did that for 4 weeks, so he rode 125 * 4 = 500 kilometers.\nThen he rode his bike 2 times a week, but for 60 kilometers each time.\nSo he rode 2 * 60 = 120 kilometers each week.\nHe did that for 3 weeks, so he rode 120 * 3 = 360 kilometers.\nThe total number of kilometers he rode is 500 + 360 = 860 kilometers.\nThe answer is 860.\n\nAnswer_36:\nJoe's bag of Halloween candy has 25 chocolate bars and 80 candied apples.\nEach chocolate bar weighs twice as much as each candied apple.\nSo each chocolate bar weighs 2 * 0.1 = 0.2 kilograms.\nThe total weight of the chocolate bars is 25 * 0.2 = 5 kilograms.\nThe total weight of the candied apples is 80 * 0.1 = 8 kilograms.\nThe total weight of the candy is 5 + 8 = 13 kilograms.\nThe answer is 13.\n\nAnswer_37:\nRose bought 4 cakes on Monday.\nOn Tuesday, she bought three times that number of cakes.\nSo she bought 4 * 3 = 12 cakes.\nOn Wednesday, she bought 5 times the number of cakes she did on Tuesday.\nSo she bought 12 * 5 = 60 cakes.\nThe total number of cakes she bought is 4 + 12 + 60 = 76.\nThe answer is 76.\n\nAnswer_38:\nTwenty dozen cups cost $1200 less than the total cost of half a dozen plates sold at $6000 each.\nTwenty dozen cups is 20 * 12 = 240 cups.\nHalf a dozen plates is 6 plates.\nThe total cost of half a dozen plates is 6 * $6000 = $36000.\nThe total cost of twenty dozen cups is $36000 - $1200 = $34800.\nThe cost of each cup is $34800 / 240 = $145.\nThe answer is $145.",
